## 1. Introduction and Central Hypothesis

### 1.1 The problem

Conventional spacecraft architecture fixes the correspondence

\[
\text{hardware} \leftrightarrow \text{function}
\]

at design time. A navigation computer is wired to navigation sensors; a thermal pump serves a fixed coolant loop; a power bus feeds a fixed set of loads. When a physical resource path fails, recovery is limited to whatever the pre-existing connectivity allows. Redundancy provides *copies*; it does not provide *alternative architectures*.

### 1.2 The proposal

We treat the spacecraft as a **survivable physical substrate** whose structure, energy, computation, sensing, propulsion, and interfaces can reorganize around the mission:

\[
\boxed{
\text{Spacecraft}
=
\text{Survivable Physical Substrate}
+
\text{Reconfigurable Functional Topology}
}
\]

The reference vehicle image is demoted to a **reference phenotype** — a morphological consequence of constraints, not an architectural premise.

### 1.3 Central hypothesis with pre-registered thresholds

Define the **physical recovery fraction**:

\[
\phi_{\mathrm{phys}}
=
\frac{N_{\mathrm{physical}}}{N_{\mathrm{faults}}}
\]

where \(N_{\mathrm{physical}}\) is the number of fault events where CRG-2 succeeds and CRG-1\(^{\mathrm{oracle}}\) fails, and \(N_{\mathrm{faults}}\) is the total number of fault events applied across all trials.

Define the **mission-success gain**:

\[
\Delta P_M = P_{M,\mathrm{CRG2}} - P_{M,\mathrm{CRG1}^{\mathrm{oracle}}}
\]

Define the **physical overhead**:

\[
O_{\mathrm{phys}} = (M_{\mathrm{phys}}, E_{\mathrm{phys}}, Q_{\mathrm{phys}}, K_{\mathrm{phys}})
\]

**Pre-registered thresholds:**

\[
\boxed{
H_{\mathrm{FRSA}} \text{ is supported only if }
\phi_{\mathrm{phys}} \geq 0.10
\text{ and }
\Delta P_M \geq 0.05
\text{ and }
\frac{\Delta P_M}{O_{\mathrm{phys}}} \geq \rho^*
}
\]

with \(\rho^* = 0.01\) per kg (at least 1% mission-success gain per 100 kg of CRG-2 overhead).

Null hypothesis:

\[
\boxed{
H_0:
\text{All useful CRG-2 recovery can be reproduced by CRG-1}^{\mathrm{oracle}}
}
\]

If \(H_0\) survives, physical role fluidity is not justified for this mission.

