### 3.2 Epistemic labels

- \(20\ \mathrm{t}\) is a **launch constraint**, not an intrinsic spacecraft dimension.
- \(4.2\ \mathrm{km/s}\) is a **design-envelope assumption**. Literature indicates the outbound LEO-to-NRHO transfer alone costs approximately 3.14–3.68 km/s, with NRHO insertion adding approximately 1.22 km/s. The return from NRHO to LEO is estimated at over 7 km/s in some sources. A round-trip mission substantially exceeds 4.2 km/s; this envelope must be decomposed by a trajectory model.

