## 15. Experiment Design

### 15.1 Stage 1: Exhaustive small fault-space

Enumerate all 1-fault and 2-fault combinations from 10 fault types:

\[
\binom{10}{1} + \binom{10}{2} = 10 + 45 = 55 \text{ combinations}
\]

For each combination, run CRG-0, CRG-1\(^{\mathrm{oracle}}\), CRG-2. Record \(N_{\mathrm{physical}}\).

### 15.2 Stage 2: Monte Carlo

| Experiment | Pattern | \(N\) |
|---|---|---:|
| A | Single faults | 3,000 |
| B | Two simultaneous | 3,000 |
| C | Three sequential | 4,000 |

### 15.3 CRG-2 overhead experiment

Allocate the 70 kg CRG-2 overhead by removing equivalent function elsewhere. Run the same fault sequences. Compare against CRG-1 with full resources.

### 15.4 Epistemic label

