FRSA-0.1 is a first-principles, falsifiable architecture for crewed spacecraft. It treats the spacecraft as a **survivable physical substrate with a reconfigurable functional topology**, derives geometry from constraints, formalizes three levels of reconfigurability, and specifies an experiment that can determine whether physical role fluidity provides recoverable mission states inaccessible to software reconfiguration alone.

