## B.5 Proposition 5 — Thermal Sink Sensitivity

### B.5.1 Formal statement

**Proposition 5.** The radiator area \(A_{\mathrm{rad}}\) required to reject heat \(Q\) at temperature \(T\) scales as:

\[
A_{\mathrm{rad}} = \frac{Q}{\epsilon \sigma (T^4 - T_{\mathrm{sink}}^4)}
\]

and the sensitivity to \(T_{\mathrm{sink}}\) is:

\[
\frac{\partial A_{\mathrm{rad}}}{\partial T_{\mathrm{sink}}} = \frac{4 \epsilon \sigma T_{\mathrm{sink}}^3 Q}{[\epsilon \sigma (T^4 - T_{\mathrm{sink}}^4)]^2}
\]

### B.5.2 Proof

**Proof.** From the Stefan–Boltzmann law:

\[
Q = \epsilon \sigma A_{\mathrm{rad}} (T^4 - T_{\mathrm{sink}}^4)
\]

Solving for \(A_{\mathrm{rad}}\):

\[
A_{\mathrm{rad}} = \frac{Q}{\epsilon \sigma (T^4 - T_{\mathrm{sink}}^4)}
\]

Differentiating with respect to \(T_{\mathrm{sink}}\):

\[
\frac{\partial A_{\mathrm{rad}}}{\partial T_{\mathrm{sink}}} = Q \cdot \frac{\partial}{\partial T_{\mathrm{sink}}} \left[ \frac{1}{\epsilon \sigma (T^4 - T_{\mathrm{sink}}^4)} \right]
\]

\[
= Q \cdot \frac{4 \epsilon \sigma T_{\mathrm{sink}}^3}{[\epsilon \sigma (T^4 - T_{\mathrm{sink}}^4)]^2}
\]

\[
= \frac{4 \epsilon \sigma T_{\mathrm{sink}}^3 Q}{[\epsilon \sigma (T^4 - T_{\mathrm{sink}}^4)]^2}
\]

\(\square\)

### B.5.3 Numerical evaluation

For \(Q = 8000\) W, \(T = 300\) K, \(\epsilon = 0.9\), \(\sigma = 5.67 \times 10^{-8}\) W/(m²·K⁴):

| \(T_{\mathrm{sink}}\) (K) | \(A_{\mathrm{rad}}\) (m²) | \(\partial A_{\mathrm{rad}}/\partial T_{\mathrm{sink}}\) (m²/K) |
|---:|---:|---:|
| 200 | 34.6 | 0.32 |
| 250 | 37.4 | 0.51 |
| 300 | 42.1 | 0.91 |
| 350 | 50.6 | 1.94 |
| 400 | 66.7 | 5.33 |

The sensitivity grows rapidly as \(T_{\mathrm{sink}} \to T\), confirming that sink temperature is a critical design parameter.

