## B.6 Proposition 6 — Mass Closure Sensitivity

### B.6.1 Formal statement

**Proposition 6.** The non-propellant mass fraction \(m_{\mathrm{nonprop}}/m_0\) is:

\[
\frac{m_{\mathrm{nonprop}}}{m_0} = 1 - \left(1 - e^{-\Delta v/(I_{sp} g_0)}\right) = e^{-\Delta v/(I_{sp} g_0)}
\]

and the sensitivity to \(\Delta v\) is:

\[
\frac{\partial}{\partial \Delta v} \left(\frac{m_{\mathrm{nonprop}}}{m_0}\right) = -\frac{1}{I_{sp} g_0} e^{-\Delta v/(I_{sp} g_0)}
\]

### B.6.2 Proof

**Proof.** From the rocket equation:

\[
\Delta v = I_{sp} g_0 \ln\frac{m_0}{m_f}
\]

\[
\frac{m_f}{m_0} = e^{-\Delta v/(I_{sp} g_0)}
\]

The propellant mass is:

\[
m_{\mathrm{prop}} = m_0 - m_f = m_0 \left(1 - e^{-\Delta v/(I_{sp} g_0)}\right)
\]

The non-propellant mass is:

\[
m_{\mathrm{nonprop}} = m_f = m_0 e^{-\Delta v/(I_{sp} g_0)}
\]

Therefore:

\[
\frac{m_{\mathrm{nonprop}}}{m_0} = e^{-\Delta v/(I_{sp} g_0)}
\]

Differentiating:

\[
\frac{\partial}{\partial \Delta v} \left(\frac{m_{\mathrm{nonprop}}}{m_0}\right) = -\frac{1}{I_{sp} g_0} e^{-\Delta v/(I_{sp} g_0)}
\]

\(\square\)

### B.6.3 Numerical evaluation

For \(I_{sp} = 450\) s, \(g_0 = 9.81\) m/s², \(m_0 = 20{,}000\) kg:

| \(\Delta v\) (m/s) | \(m_{\mathrm{nonprop}}\) (kg) | \(m_{\mathrm{prop}}\) (kg) | \(\partial m_{\mathrm{nonprop}}/\partial \Delta v\) (kg/(m/s)) |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 3000 | 10,140 | 9,860 | −2.30 |
| 4200 | 7,720 | 12,280 | −1.75 |
| 5000 | 6,440 | 13,560 | −1.46 |
| 6000 | 5,140 | 14,860 | −1.17 |
| 7000 | 4,100 | 15,900 | −0.93 |

**Interpretation:** Each additional 1 km/s of \(\Delta v\) reduces non-propellant mass by approximately 1.5–2.3 t for this vehicle class.

