# Appendix L — Analysis Pipeline — Pareto and Sensitivity

## L.1 Pareto Frontier Construction

### L.1.1 Algorithm

```python
def pareto_frontier(points: List[np.ndarray]) -> List[np.ndarray]:
    frontier = []
    for p in points:
        dominated = False
        for q in points:
            if all(q <= p) and any(q < p):
                dominated = True
                break
        if not dominated:
            frontier.append(p)
    return frontier
```

### L.1.2 Practical dominance with tolerance

```python
def practical_dominance(p, q, epsilon):
    return all(p[i] <= q[i] + epsilon[i] for i in range(len(p)))
```

## L.2 Sensitivity Analysis

### L.2.1 Tornado chart

For each parameter \(x_i\), compute:

\[
\Delta J_i = J(x_i^{\mathrm{high}}) - J(x_i^{\mathrm{low}})
\]

Rank parameters by \(|\Delta J_i|\).

### L.2.2 Sobol indices

For global sensitivity:

\[
S_i = \frac{\mathrm{Var}_{x_i}(\mathbb{E}[J | x_i])}{\mathrm{Var}(J)}
\]

\[
S_{ij} = \frac{\mathrm{Var}_{x_{ij}}(\mathbb{E}[J | x_i, x_j])}{\mathrm{Var}(J)} - S_i - S_j
\]

## L.3 Statistical Tests

### L.3.1 Difference in proportions

\[
z = \frac{\hat p_2 - \hat p_1}{\sqrt{\hat p(1-\hat p)(1/n_1 + 1/n_2)}}
\]

where \(\hat p = (n_1 \hat p_1 + n_2 \hat p_2)/(n_1 + n_2)\).

### L.3.2 Confidence interval

\[
\mathrm{CI}_{95\%} = \hat p \pm 1.96 \sqrt{\frac{\hat p(1-\hat p)}{n}}
\]

