# Appendix T — Reliability Model — Bayesian Framework

## T.1 Component Reliability

For each component \(i\):

\[
R_i(t) = e^{-\lambda_i t}
\]

where \(\lambda_i\) is the failure rate.

## T.2 System Reliability

### T.2.1 Series system

\[
R_{\mathrm{series}} = \prod_i R_i
\]

### T.2.2 Parallel system

\[
R_{\mathrm{parallel}} = 1 - \prod_i (1 - R_i)
\]

### T.2.3 Reconfigurable system

\[
R_{\mathrm{reconfig}} = P(\text{at least one feasible configuration})
\]

## T.3 Bayesian Updating

Prior:

\[
\lambda \sim \mathrm{Gamma}(\alpha, \beta)
\]

Posterior after \(n\) failures in \(T\) hours:

\[
\lambda | \mathrm{data} \sim \mathrm{Gamma}(\alpha + n, \beta + T)
\]

## T.4 Credible Interval

\[
P(\lambda_{\mathrm{low}} \leq \lambda \leq \lambda_{\mathrm{high}} | \mathrm{data}) = 0.95
\]

## T.5 Application to FRSA

For CRG-2, the additional switches introduce new failure modes. The reliability model must account for:

\[
\lambda_{\mathrm{CRG2}} = \lambda_{\mathrm{base}} + \lambda_{\mathrm{switch}}
\]

The experiment measures whether the recovery benefit exceeds the reliability cost.

